# Build output and fuzzer-produced data. Corpora are regenerated by scheduled
# runs and are never committed (Section 11.3: binary fixtures stay out of the
# repository).
#
# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. This crate is excluded from the
# workspace, so the root lockfile never covers it; ignoring its own lock meant
# every fresh CI checkout re-resolved the fuzzer dependencies and ran their
# build scripts on whatever the registry served that day, outside every
# advisory, licence and source gate (2026-07-29 audit). The lock is committed,
# `cargo xtask fuzz` verifies it with `--locked` before fuzzing, and
# `cargo xtask supply-chain` checks this graph explicitly.
target/
corpus/
artifacts/
coverage/
